## Building on Linux

```sh
make clean && make && make test
```

## Building on Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64)

**Recommended:** open **MSYS2 UCRT64** from the Start menu:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/yes-toto
make clean && make && make test
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`yes-toto` or `yes-toto.exe`). Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, and CMD.

### Git Bash caveat

Git Bash can build if **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is early on `PATH`** (before Anaconda). Otherwise `gcc --version` may work while `cc1` fails silently (DLL load order). Prefer UCRT64 shell or:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- `fill_buffer()` is `static inline` in `yes_toto.h` — compiled into `yes_toto_write.c` and each test TU.
- Tests **do not** link `src/*.c`; they only exercise `fill_buffer()` via the header.
- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c`.
